# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Aeris — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in whatever you want to use.
# Everything below is optional; the app runs with no secrets at all.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Analytics (optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# Google Analytics 4 measurement ID. Leave blank to disable analytics.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# --- OpenSky Network (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# OAuth2 client credentials for the server-side trace fallback
# (src/lib/trails/source/server-trace-service.ts). Without these, Aeris
# still works — the trace service falls back to public adsb.lol / readsb
# endpoints. Provide both values or neither.
#
# Create a client at https://opensky-network.org/my-opensky (Account → API).
# OPENSKY_CLIENT_ID=
# OPENSKY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- OpenAIP (optional) -----------------------------------------------------
# API key for the airspace vector-tile proxy
# (src/app/api/airspace-tiles/route.ts). Without this, the airspace
# overlay toggle will produce empty responses; flight rendering is
# unaffected. Get a key from https://www.openaip.net (Account → API keys).
#
# Remember: OpenAIP data is CC BY-NC 4.0 — attribution is already rendered
# in-app but non-commercial use is on you.
# OPENAIP_API_KEY=

# --- ATC source registry (optional) -----------------------------------------
# Add authorized community or self-hosted Icecast-compatible streams to the
# built-in LiveATC source. This JSON is server configuration, not a secret, and
# its stream URLs are sent to browsers. Provider/source IDs must be unique;
# feedIds must match existing stable feed IDs; URLs must use HTTPS; lower
# priority numbers are preferred (LiveATC uses 100); and cors must truthfully
# describe whether Web Audio may analyze the cross-origin stream.
#
# Redeploy/restart after changing this value. Aeris validates it at startup and
# adds its stream origins to Content Security Policy. Invalid configuration
# intentionally prevents the app from starting.
#
# Icecast example (expanded and explained in README.md):
# ATC_CUSTOM_SOURCES_JSON={"providers":[{"id":"community-jfk","label":"JFK Community Receiver","attributionUrl":"https://radio.example.org/about"}],"sources":[{"id":"community-jfk-tower","providerId":"community-jfk","feedIds":["kjfk-tower"],"streamUrl":"https://radio.example.org:8443/kjfk-tower.mp3","priority":50,"cors":true}]}

# --- Notes ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public ADS-B providers (airplanes.live, adsb.lol) are called directly
# from the browser with CORS, so they do not need credentials.
